  Author: "sliptonic"
  License: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  Name: "Medium-Density Fibreboard (MDF)"
  Description: >-
    Medium-Density Fibreboard (MDF), an engineered wood product composed of
    wood fibers and binding resin pressed together under heat and pressure.
    Typical composition: ~82% wood fibre, ~9% urea-formaldehyde resin, ~8%
    water, ~1% paraffin wax.
    Density, modulus of elasticity (MOE), and modulus of rupture (MOR):
    Wikipedia article "Medium-density fibreboard" (CC-BY-SA-4.0), accessed
    2026-03. Density value 700 kg/m^3 is the centre of the standard MDF range
    (600-800 kg/m^3); high-density (HDF) and low-density (LDF) variants
    deviate substantially.
    Thermal conductivity: typical value for MDF panel (widely-published
    construction data).
    Machinability data sourced verbatim from FreeCAD core 'MDF.FCMat'
    (Jonas Bähr, CC-BY-3.0, from Zerspanung von Holz und Holzwerkstoffen
    ISBN 978-3-446-47769-8) using B.Ettelt's cutting-force model adapted
    to FreeCAD's Machinability schema.
  SourceURL: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medium-density_fibreboard"
  Tags:
    - "Wood"
    - "Engineered Wood"
    - "MDF"
    - "Fibreboard"
    - "Composite"
